ute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-34248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34248" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=7 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the third equation by $-1$ and adding the result to the first equation we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{1} & =7-4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow,  we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ into the third equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ 3(3)-{x}_{2} & =4 \\\\ -{x}_{2} & =4-9 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5$ into the second equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =9 \\\\ -2(3)+3(5) & =9 \\\\ -6+15 & =9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=5,$ which means\n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+5{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3+5=8.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-73981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third  equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} & =-16\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+{x}_{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ (-2)+2(3) & =3 \\\\ 4 & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c