\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0=4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first equation is a false statement. Hence,the system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34242" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-34242" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34242" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34242" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the resulting equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =-5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3(-5) & =1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1} & =-14 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=7$ and ${x}_{2}=-5$ into the third equation and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 3(7)+5(-5) & =-4 \\\\ -4 & =-4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=7$ and ${x}_{2}=-5,$ which means\n\n$$\n7{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7+(-5)=2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-105166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "5"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-7 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equation we get\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{2}=-8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=4$ into the first equation yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1}-(4) & =-7 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-7+4 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} & =6 \\\\ 2(-3)+3(4) & =6 \\\\ 6 & =6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-3$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-3+4=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-73952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-73952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-9 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-3 \\\\ {x}_{3}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-1.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2,{x}_{3}=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(-1) & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-5 & =-1 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=4$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=-1,$ which means \n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}-{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=4+(-2)-(-1)=3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-74028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "7"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -5{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ -21{x}_{2} \\\\ -12{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ 14{x}_{3} \\\\ 9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -5{x}_{1}-21{x}_{2}+14{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -21 & 14 & 8 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 9 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1 & 18 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=18 \\\\ 0=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=-1$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-105172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "17"] ["math" "19"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "7"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-105172" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ -11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -18 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-11{x}_{3}=-18 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -11 & -18\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -15 & -30\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{15}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=5 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this value into  the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-2(2)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, by substituting ${x}_{2}=-2$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+(-2)+3(2) & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1}+4 & =5 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=1$, ${x}_{2}=-2$, and ${x}_{3}=2,$ which means \n\n$$\n{a}_{1}-2{a}_{2}+2{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1+(-2)+2=1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74032" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=5.$ Substituting this value in the second and first equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{2}-2(5)=-6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=4 \\\\  & {x}_{1}+5=8\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=3$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=5,$ which means \n\n$$\n3{a}_{1}+4{a}_{2}+5{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+4+5=12.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-74046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "15"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-74046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=-6 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 13\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ 0=13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=13$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34566" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "277a1276fba71699bb031c7c6ec50d19a68b1ac54e98c9c2b1323f94e6b8525b"} {"question" "q-34566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-25"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-36"] ["math" "5"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "q-34566" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/state.json" "file_sha256" "ea05d4ca7c99bd689276f3933548e7224fd652ee439272559ce790fdf89f8ebd"} {"question" "e-4789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $s,$ if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/df62636427555a986454d8d2787e110eb664771f5a74a38fdaa99ec593643729.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4789.json" "file_sha256" "2f2b238e048cec206630c25379400cd06343af81483b5983561a7d7c4beb883c"} {"question" "e-4789" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+s{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4789.json" "file_sha256" "2f2b238e048cec206630c25379400cd06343af81483b5983561a7d7c4beb883c"} {"question" "e-4790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\mathbf{x},$ if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/0e6491c477a442fc9dae1462413d593815a6761393ad3a0d2f8d72de665a7c93.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4790.json" "file_sha256" "5390b86fa6c93a11f2212613512364496bbcd3e59bca58363af1429af397957e"} {"question" "e-4790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2x & =b \\\\ 2x & =b-a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}(b-a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}([\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4790.json" "file_sha256" "5390b86fa6c93a11f2212613512364496bbcd3e59bca58363af1429af397957e"} {"question" "e-4791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/e9e0ea8fb6e9ba5f4595f15efe4f04e93db373dbc020f5672db34d5a3c12024b.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then what is $x_1+x_2?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4791.json" "file_sha256" "af5ffa41d7cdec673526d87c837b7923dffc92c9ac5b6d0070c82145d07aed14"} {"question" "e-4791" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2  = \\mathbf d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}=-5 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain $x_1=5,$ which we substitute into the first equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 4(5)+{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3(5)+(-15) & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15,$ which means\n\n$$\n5 \\mathbf{c_1}-15 \\mathbf{c_2} = \\mathbf{d}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2=5-15=-10.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-4791.json" "file_sha256" "af5ffa41d7cdec673526d87c837b7923dffc92c9ac5b6d0070c82145d07aed14"} {"question" "e-6191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the vectors\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/4749f1e50cf7768f39d26737bfce4d9e8e85d5b350f4bc9844a358cd4c3c5cc0.png)\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf b,$ then what is $x_1+x_2+x_3?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-6191.json" "file_sha256" "69790720315e2794dcc498c28fc23d3b0345d43ca733102d0c16b1a4c4f323bd"} {"question" "e-6191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/assets/a4e5c5eba6d2d8b30955668d47bb2a131c702cc7ec62ef7dada9ed9ad60d8182.png)\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ {x}_{3}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3.\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042052/example-6191.json" "file_sha256" "69790720315e2794dcc498c28fc23d3b0345d43ca733102d0c16b1a4c4f323bd"}] "usage" {"e-4790" [] "e-4789" [] "q-34248" [] "q-34566" [] "q-34249" [] "e-4791" [] "e-6191" []} "basis" 1627 "retractions" [[17592186120244 :question/problem "Find $l$, if $5a_{1} + la_{2} = b$ and\n\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 19\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186120243 :question/problem "Find $x$, if $4a + 6x = b$ and\n\n$a = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186120282 :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}, a_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nIf $x_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} + x_{3}a_{3} = b$, then what is $x_{1} + x_{2} + x_{3}$?"] [17592186119543 :question/problem "Find $s$, if $3\\mathbf{a_1}+s\\mathbf{a_2} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186119543 :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $s$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3a_{1} + sa_{2} &= b \\\\\n3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + s\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\ns\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} - 3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\ns\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $s=4$."] [17592186119544 :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{x}$, if $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ and\n$\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186119544 :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $\\mathbf{x}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na + 2x &= b \\\\\n2x &= b - a \\\\\nx &= \\frac{1}{2}(b - a) \\\\\nx &= \\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\nx &= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nx &= \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119545 :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2 = \\mathbf d$, then what is $x_1+x_2$?"] [17592186119545 :question/worked-solution "If\n\n$$\nx_1 \\mathbf{c}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{c}_2 = \\mathbf d\n$$\n\nthen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}4x_{1} + x_{2} \\\\ -x_{1} \\\\ 3x_{1} + x_{2}\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{4x_{1} + x_{2} = 5; - x_{1} =-5; 3x_{1} + x_{2} = 0\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain $x_1=5$, which we substitute into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4x_{1} + x_{2} &= 5 \\\\\n4(5) + x_{2} &= 5 \\\\\nx_{2} &= -15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15$ into the third equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x_{1} + x_{2} &= 0 \\\\\n3(5) + (-15) &= 0 \\\\\n0 &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement.\n\nSo the solution of the system is $x_1=5$ and $x_2=-15$, which means\n\n$$\n5 \\mathbf{c_1}-15 \\mathbf{c_2} = \\mathbf{d}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2=5-15=-10\n$$"] [17592186119593 :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nIf $x_1 \\mathbf{a}_1 + x_2\\mathbf{a}_2 + x_3\\mathbf{a}_3 = \\mathbf b$, then what is $x_1+x_2+x_3$?"] [17592186119593 :question/worked-solution "Since $\\mathbf{b}$ is a linear combination of vectors $\\mathbf{a_1}, \\,\\mathbf{a_2}$ and $\\mathbf{a_3}$ with coefficients $x_1,\\, x_2$ and $x_3$, respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1}a_{1} + x_{2}a_{2} + x_{3}a_{3} &= b \\\\\nx_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + x_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} + x_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ x_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}x_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -x_{2}\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}x_{3} \\\\ 2x_{3} \\\\ 3x_{3}\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}x_{2} + x_{3} \\\\ x_{1} + 2x_{3} \\\\ -x_{2} + 3x_{3}\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{x_{2} + x_{3} = 1; x_{1} + 2x_{3} = 1; - x_{2} + 3x_{3} = 7\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM &= \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}R_{1} & ↔R_{2} \\\\ ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & R_{3}\\end{vmatrix}:=R_{3} + R_{2} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\mid R_{3} \\mid:=\\frac{1}{4}R_{3} \\\\\n&= ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{x_{1} + 2x_{3} = 1; x_{2} + x_{3} = 1; x_{3} = 2\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get $x_3 = 2$. Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_2+(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_2 = -1\n$$\n\nand substituting $x_3=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx_1+2(2) = 1 \\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x_1 = -3\n$$\n\nSo the solution of the system is\n\n$$\nx_1=-3, x_2=-1, x_3=2\n$$\n\nwhich means\n\n$$\n-3 \\mathbf{a_1}- \\mathbf{a_2} +2 \\mathbf{a_3}= \\mathbf{b}\n$$\n\nConsequently,\n\n$$\nx_1+x_2+x_3=-3-1+2=-2\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186117959 17592186117960 17592186117961 17592186117962 17592186117963 17592186117965 17592186117966 17592186117967 17592186117968 17592186117969 17592186118168 17592186118169 17592186118170 17592186118171 17592186118172] "immutable_fields" [[17592186117958 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117958 :answer-field/id] [17592186117958 :answer-field/key] [17592186117958 :answer-field/type] [17592186117964 :answer-field/correct] [1759